{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "label": "managementRoutes(system, cluster, options)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Baut einen Route-Baum betrieblicher Endpunkte und gibt sonst nichts zurueck - Port und Host sind keine Settings, sie gehen an system.http(port, { host })."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutesoptions", "label": "ManagementRoutesOptionsType", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "enableLeaveEndpoint, enableDownEndpoint, enableMetricsEndpoint, auth, ipAllowlist, authProtectHealth."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_healthcheckregistry", "label": "HealthCheckRegistry / healthChecksOf(system)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die Checks liegen auf dem ActorSystem, nicht auf dem Route-Baum: Komponenten, denen ein Gesundheitssignal gehoert, registrieren sich beim Start - lange bevor irgendwer einen Route-Baum baut - und eigene Checks kommen auf dasselbe Objekt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_framework_checks", "label": "Framework-Checks: actor-system, cluster-membership, cluster-transport", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die beiden Readiness-Checks installiert Cluster.join."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_separater_port", "label": "Warum ein separater Port (8558)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die Management-Endpunkte legen internen Zustand offen - Cluster-Mitgliederadressen, Metrikwerte; sie oeffentlich zu exponieren ist ein Sicherheitsrisiko. In K8s ist das per-Pod: Probes treffen :8558 vom Kubelet, kein Service exponiert es extern."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_k8s_probes", "label": "K8s-Probe-Verdrahtung", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "readinessProbe auf /ready, livenessProbe auf /health, beide auf Port 8558."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_mounten_in_bestehenden_server", "label": "In einen bestehenden Server mounten", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zwei Gruende: es gibt schon einen HTTP-Server, oder eine Single-Node-App ohne Cluster, bei der Health-Checks allein den Extra-Port nicht rechtfertigen. Auf dem oeffentlichen Port exponiert das internen Zustand erneut."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_management_overview_managementroutesoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/management/overview